  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Any player may request a brief pause; the table protects private game information and waits before actions that require that player.\", \"decision\": \"How should players signal a need for a personal break?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nPlayers place a pause card beside the board when they need a break, and the table stops at the next safe point. A visible signal communicates the need without requiring a personal explanation in front of the group.\nPlayers ask aloud for a personal break, and the table agrees a convenient immediate pause before they leave. A direct request makes the interruption clear and lets everyone confirm which game action will resume afterward.\nThe teacher checks for break needs at agreed milestones, while players can still request an earlier pause. Regular invitations make it easier to accept a break without removing anyone’s ability to ask when needed."
    }
  ],
